WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.998
Every animal has to eat. But where
does its food really come from?

2
00:00:09.218 --> 00:00:14.697
Follow the food back, and every chain
starts at the same place: a plant.

3
00:00:15.197 --> 00:00:19.841
A plant does not eat. It makes its
own food from sunlight, water and air.

4
00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:23.219
Because it produces food,
we call it a producer.

5
00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:26.876
Grass is a producer. It does
not eat anything at all.

6
00:00:27.096 --> 00:00:32.251
Every food chain starts with a plant,
and the plant's food starts with the Sun.

7
00:00:32.751 --> 00:00:35.584
An animal cannot make food. It has to eat.

8
00:00:35.804 --> 00:00:40.076
A rabbit eats the grass. An
animal that eats is a consumer.

9
00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:43.872
A fox eats the rabbit.
The fox is a consumer too.

10
00:00:44.092 --> 00:00:47.946
Grass, rabbit, fox. A food
chain shows who eats whom.

11
00:00:48.446 --> 00:00:53.323
Plants are producers. Animals are
consumers. That is the whole rule.

12
00:00:53.543 --> 00:00:57.583
An oak tree, seagrass and a
dandelion all make their own food.

13
00:00:57.803 --> 00:01:03.190
An owl, a fish and a rabbit cannot.
They have to eat, so they are consumers.

14
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.868
A cow makes milk, but it eats
grass. Eating makes it a consumer.

15
00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:13.569
We draw a food chain with arrows.
Grass, arrow, rabbit, arrow, fox.

16
00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:18.526
The arrow means is eaten by.
Grass is eaten by the rabbit.

17
00:01:18.746 --> 00:01:22.090
It points from the food to
the animal that eats it.

18
00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:26.815
So the arrow goes from the grass
to the rabbit, never the other way.

19
00:01:27.035 --> 00:01:31.446
A drawing like this is a diagram:
a model of who eats whom.

20
00:01:31.946 --> 00:01:37.148
Now make a chain you can hold. Draw
grass, a rabbit and a fox on three cards.

21
00:01:37.368 --> 00:01:42.012
Tie the rabbit card under the grass
card, and the fox under the rabbit.

22
00:01:42.232 --> 00:01:47.758
Hold up the grass card. The whole chain
hangs from it. That is a physical model.

23
00:01:47.978 --> 00:01:52.622
Now let go of the grass card,
and watch. The whole chain falls.

24
00:01:52.842 --> 00:01:59.158
No grass, no rabbit. No rabbit, no fox.
Every link needs the one before it.

25
00:01:59.658 --> 00:02:03.977
Spray the weeds and the plants
die. No plants, no caterpillars.

26
00:02:04.197 --> 00:02:10.327
No caterpillars, and the birds that eat them
go hungry. Three links gone, from one spray.

27
00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:17.699
Oil in the pond blocks the light. The pondweed
dies, then the snails, the frogs, the heron.

28
00:02:17.919 --> 00:02:23.956
Plant a hedge and you plant a producer. Insects
come, then birds, and a new chain starts.

29
00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:28.773
Science shows us what our actions
do to the living things around us.

30
00:02:29.273 --> 00:02:33.453
A plant is the producer. It
makes its own food from sunlight.

31
00:02:33.673 --> 00:02:36.970
Every animal is a consumer,
because it has to eat.

32
00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:42.670
The arrow means is eaten by. Draw
the chain, or hold it on cards.

33
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:48.231
Take the plant away and the whole chain
falls. That is why what we do matters.
